{
  "`masterDetail` gives every row details of its own: the expand column opens a row to show what `template` makes for it — here another grid over a data source of its own, filtered by the customer's key — in a row across the grid that stays in place while the columns scroll sideways. The details are made the first time they show and kept while the row is open; they go when the row leaves the data, or with the grid. The list stays virtual: each detail is measured as it is drawn (and again when its content changes size), so the scroll bar, the rows after it and moving to a row stay right, and the rows themselves are still a small pool.": "",
  "The expand column, after the status and check box columns and pinned like them: the user opens and closes the details. Off, they open programmatically only.": "",
  "What a row’s details hold: a component (another `DataGrid`, a `FormLayout`, `Tabs` …), an element or a text. Made the first time the details show. `ctx`: `row` (the row itself) and `rowIndex`, both read again in getters when the row shows another one and on `grid.repaint()` or `grid.repaintRows(keys)`, `key`, `grid`, `collapse()`.": "",
  "Every row starts open. Changing it, `enabled` or `template` opens or closes every row again.": "",
  "Whether a row has details; a row without has no arrow, and `expandRow` leaves it closed. New rows not saved yet have none.": "",
  "A closed row keeps what its details hold and shows it as it was when it opens again; off, closing disposes it.": "",
  "Paged grid: the details of the page left keep what they hold while the user pages (up to `keepLimit`); off, another page or page size disposes them, and they are made again when their page shows. A row stays open either way.": "",
  "Details out of view that keep their content (open ones, and closed ones with `keepDetails`); past it the ones seen longest ago are disposed, and made again when they show.": "",
  "the content’s": "",
  "A height of their own in pixels, the content scrolling inside; a function gives each row its own.": "",
  "What details count as before they are drawn and measured, while none is; then the average of those measured. Only the scroll bar uses it.": "",
  "Width of the expand column, in pixels.": "",
  "Keys on the expand cell that open and close the details.": "",
  "Right on the expand cell of a closed row opens it, Left on an open one closes it; otherwise they move as on any cell.": "",
  "Open rows are kept by key: sorting, the filters, the search, grouping and paging leave them open, and a row that comes back after a filter opens again. Selecting and editing the rows work as before; a row edited in the edit form keeps its details under the form. Copying and exporting leave the details out, and the saved layout does not keep which rows are open.": "",
  "Tabs and forms in the details": "",
  "The details can hold any component. Here they are tabs: a read-only `FormLayout` with the customer, and a list of its orders made when the tab is first shown — the row takes its height, the rows after it move. `canExpand` leaves the customers without orders without an arrow; `ctx.collapse()` closes a row from inside its details; the buttons call `expandAllRows()` and `collapseAllRows()`.": "",
  "Keyboard and accessibility": "",
  "The arrow is a button with `aria-expanded` and `aria-controls`; the row says `aria-expanded` too. A row's details are a row of their own in the grid's reading order (`aria-owns`), right after it and counted in `aria-rowindex` and `aria-rowcount`, with one cell across the columns named “Details of row 3” (`gridDetailsOf`, `gridDetails` for the arrow and its column; both in `uiLocale` and the grid's `texts`).": "",
  "On the expand cell: opens or closes the row’s details.": "",
  "On the expand cell: Right opens a closed row, Left closes an open one; then they move to the next cell. Mirrored right to left.": "",
  "Move from row to row; a row’s details are passed over.": "",
  "On a row whose details show: into the details, to their first stop. With details on the screen Tab otherwise leaves the grid, as Shift+Tab does from a row.": "",
  "Moves through their content; from the last stop it leaves the grid.": "",
  "Back to the row the details belong to (Escape the content does not use itself).": "",
  "Into the content, to its first stop.": "",
  "A row’s details are about to open or close, by the user or programmatically; `cancel` keeps them as they are. The same events as for groups (`kind: 'group'`).": "",
  "They opened or closed.": "",
  "A row’s details were drawn for a row.": "",
  "A `masterDetail` option was assigned through `grid.masterDetail`.": "",
  "Opens or closes a row’s details by its key, as the arrow does (the events come, `cancel` holds); a row not loaded, or one without details, does not.": "",
  "Whether a row’s details are open. Reactive.": "",
  "Opens or closes every row’s details at once, without row events (as `expandAll()` does for groups).": "",
  "A row's details are listed right after it, `rowType: 'detail'`, with its index and key.": ""
}
